1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:11,450
Markets keep moving, but your liquidity occupies a chosen place. Kelpie begins with that tension: a changing price, and the boundaries you decide to set around it.

2
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:27,275
Concentrated liquidity works within a selected price range. When price leaves those boundaries, the practical question is not simply where to move, but when movement is justified.

3
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:42,425
Kelpie is a concentrated-liquidity manager on Sui. You choose the pool, the range width, and the delay, establishing the parameters that shape how your position can be managed.

4
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:58,400
Supported venues include SuiDex V3 and Cetus, but the venue is fixed when the position opens. Management does not move that position between exchanges as conditions change.

5
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:12,700
Ownership stays with you; the keeper receives bounded management authority. The distinction matters: permission to carry out defined actions is not permission to take over your position.

6
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:26,000
Range width defines the span of prices you select. It is a practical parameter to examine, rather than a promise that your liquidity will remain in range.

7
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:41,550
Your chosen delay adds a condition of time. A price moving outside the range is not, by itself, permission for Kelpie to immediately move the position elsewhere.

8
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:56,350
If price returns before the delay has elapsed, that departure has not satisfied the waiting condition. The boundary is real, but crossing it is not enough alone.

9
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:12,975
Only an out-of-range condition that persists through your chosen delay permits this re-range. That is a threshold for bounded management, not a requirement to chase every market movement.

10
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:27,425
When permitted, the position can be re-ranged at the same width, single-sided, without a swap. The range changes location; its span is preserved, rather than widened to follow.

11
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:43,525
Single-sided means the re-range uses one side of the pool pair, without swapping between the assets. This is a constrained repositioning mechanism, not an unrestricted trading strategy.

12
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:58,500
These limits make the process understandable, not certain. Kelpie does not promise returns or keep price inside your range; market exposure remains part of providing concentrated liquidity.

13
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:14,200
Memory gives those parameter choices a past to examine. Kelpie records hourly pool observations, creating historical context for comparing settings instead of relying only on the present moment.

14
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:28,300
An observation is a record, not an instruction to act. Hourly memory supports historical comparison; it does not mean that positions must move, or that archives publish every hour.

15
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:43,200
At midnight, the daily records seal. That daily boundary turns accumulated observations into a closed record, separating the rhythm of collecting history from the rhythm of preserving it.

16
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:57,200
Those sealed daily records go onto Walrus within the week, not every hour. Keeping these schedules distinct helps you understand what the archive contains, and when it arrives.

17
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:14,200
Historical comparison lets you examine different widths and delays against past pool observations. It can inform a decision, but yesterday's behavior cannot establish what tomorrow's market will do.

18
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:27,025
Use Kelpie's guide and backtest to examine the mechanism before choosing parameters. Ask what each setting permits, how long it waits, and whether those limits fit your intentions.

19
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:43,175
The practical payoff is a clearer division of responsibility: you choose the boundaries, the keeper operates within them, and recorded history helps you compare choices without promising the future.

20
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:58,650
The Water Horse crosses from midnight into pale water, its amber thread still unbroken. Kelpie leaves you with a grounded starting point: choose deliberately, understand the rules, retain control.
